{
  "requirement": "TBV owns the model conversation, supported backend integrations, tool\ndispatch, and structured submission used by its ask builder.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only structural clause is \"TBV owns the model conversation, supported backend integrations, tool dispatch, and structured submission used by its ask builder.\" This is a delegation obligation. An alternative could hand the loop to a third-party agent runner, such as rig's agent or tool-calling loop. It could produce the same answers but would not be owned by TBV. So the clause is structural, and the roots cover it.\n\n- **Conversation and submission:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P,%20T>]#2/fn[run_with_domain_tools]` builds the opening `CompletionRequest`, including the prompt and prefix. It creates the `GraphSession` and `SessionTools`, then calls TBV's own `converse` loop in `agent.rs`. `converse` drives the loop and checks submissions. The `GraphSession` `Conversation` implementation supplies the `submission_tool` and `submitted_value` handling.\n- **Tool dispatch:** `GraphSession` and `SessionTools` dispatch each tool call, including `read_node` and `outgoing_edges`, to the domain tools. They are reached from the marked `run_with_domain_tools` through `converse`, so they need no separate marker.\n- **Backend integrations:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#impl[RigProvider]/fn[connect]` builds the Bedrock, OpenAI and Ollama backends. It uses rig only as a completion transport, wrapped in TBV's `RigProvider`. `RigProvider`'s `complete` method, which `converse` reaches through the `CompletionProvider` trait, issues a single completion call. It also applies Bedrock options, normalizes Bedrock client calls and places cache checkpoints. It does not run a conversation loop or dispatch tools.\n\nAll the structural obligations map to source reachable from the two supplied roots, so no further marker is needed.\n\nbehavioral: `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent` is an umbrella requirement. It says TBV owns four things: the model conversation, the supported backend integrations, tool dispatch, and structured submission. Its details are refined by `submission`, `submission.*`, `tool_agent.isolation`, `tool_agent.provider_failure`, `fixed_tools`, `with_tool`, `domain_tool_dispatch` and the config requirements. Those obligations are assessed under their own requirements, so I did not reassess them here.\n\nThe reviewed tests cover each obligation the umbrella states:\n\n- **Conversation ownership:**\n  - `tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` asserts the system prompt, the user message content and order, and the `submit_result` schema in the request.\n  - `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` asserts that the second request carries the earlier tool output.\n  - `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[typed_client_calls_preserve_order_and_native_history]` asserts that response order and native history are preserved.\n- **Backend integrations:**\n  - OpenAI and Ollama are tested end to end against local transports. These tests check the model, option mapping, the tool list, the `submit_result` schema, authorization, and delivery of tool results (`supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport`, `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat`).\n  - Bedrock needs a real AWS service, so it is tested through `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_native_option_types_are_checked_and_only_max_tokens_is_defaulted]`, `cache_checkpoints_are_requested_for_caching_models` and `typed_client_calls_preserve_order_and_native_history`. This is acceptable.\n- **Tool dispatch:**\n  - `tests.rs#fn[application_tools_preserve_graph_tools_in_the_same_conversation]` asserts the delivered results from `outgoing_edges`, `read_node`, `get_next_page` and the application `increment` tool, plus the recorded dependencies.\n  - `application_tool_factories_create_fresh_state_for_each_agent_call` asserts fresh tool state per call.\n- **Structured submission:** the typed `submit_result` answer is parsed and returned and its fingerprint is stored (`behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer`). Concurrent calls keep their submissions apart (`concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`, `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces`).\n\nI found no behavioral obligation in the text that lacks a test with a relevant assertion.",
